      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T13:26:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t want to reopen the locking question, which I understand is settled for A16. \n\nFrankly speaking I am not sure if the `GICR_PENDBASER`, `GICR_PROPBASER` and `GICR_CTLR` could be hardened properly without taking a global lock on all redistributors... But if you have some idea how I would be curious how. However indeed not for A16.\n\n\n\u003e Could we narrow the deny instead, so that with priv NULL we forward the offsets that have no emu_handler and RAZ/WI only the handled ones? \n\nYes. PTAL. I\u0027ve modified the changes to have to sets of handlers - pre init and post init. Post init stay as is. However the new pre init would handle the registers that we could not handle as suggested as RAZ/WI. For `GICR_INVLPIR` and `GICR_INVALLR` we don\u0027t need state, so they would be already hardened. \n\nI made`GICR_CTLR` read `RWP\u003d1` write ignored pre init. However I am not very confident if `RWP\u003d1` alone is a good idea, yet RAZ would be worse (?). At least this way we signal the host that there\u0027s something going on with GICR and should wait.",
