      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, the split is what I was after, and forwarding the offsets with no handler is the part that matters.\n\nOn RWP\u003d1, I think it is the right call. gic_do_wait_for_rwp polls for a second and then prints \"RWP timeout, gone fishing\" and carries on, so a CPU that polls inside the window gets a stall and a log line rather than a wrong answer. RAZ is what would be worse: the driver reads no write pending, carries on, and its model of the redistributor quietly stops matching the hardware.\n\nAgreed the global lock is not an A16 problem.",
